n(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D010006\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000062 \"Skeletogenic cell that secretes osteoid, is capable of producing mineralized (hydroxyapatite) matrix, is located adjacent to or within osteoid tissue, and arises from the transformation of a preosteoblast cell.\")\n4556:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000081 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000988 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0008015)))\n4591:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000084 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000542 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0002456)))\n4655:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000091 \"Markers: Mouse: F4/80+, CD11b-low, CD68+, sialoadhesin+, CD163/SRCR+; role or process: immune, antigen-presentation, clearance of senescent erythrocytes, iron metabolism. Kupffer cells are also reportedly C3aR-positive, CD14-low, CD54-positive, CD88-positive, and CD284-positive. They are also capable of producing IL-1, IL-6, TNF-alpha, nitric oxide, PGD2, PGE2, PGF2alpha, and TXA2.\")\n4657:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000091 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000864 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0001025 obo:UBERON_0001281) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001813) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001925) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000002064) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0034102) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0015016 obo:PR_000001012)))\n4670:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000092 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000766 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001474) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:PR_000001850) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:PR_000001937) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:PR_000001944) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:PR_000007597) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:PR_000011178) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001954) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000002062) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0045453)))\n4694:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000094 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000766 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:GO_0030141) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:CL_4030046 obo:PR_000001002) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:CL_4030046 obo:PR_000001020) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:CL_4030046 obo:PR_000001024) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:CL_4030046 obo:PR_000001084) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001012) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001332) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001969) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0008015)))\n4719:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000096 \"Neutrophils are also capable of secreting GRO-alpha, IL-1beta, IL-1ra, IL-3, IL-12, IP-10, MIG, MIP-1alpha, MIP-1beta, TGF-beta, TNF-alpha, VEGF, and anti-microbial peptides. They can positively influence the chemotaxis of basophils, T-cells, monocytes, macrophages, dendritic cells, and other neutrophils. Neutrophils are also CD35-positive, CD64-positive, CD89-positive, CD184-positive, and fMLP receptor-positive Ly-6G-positive (mouse), TLR2-low, TLR4-low, and lineage-negative (CD2, CD3, CD5, CD9, CD19, CD36, CD49d, CD56, CD61, CD235a (glycophorin-A)).\")\n4721:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000096 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000775 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:CL_0017500) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:GO_0070820) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:GO_0005634 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000053 obo:PATO_0001979))) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:CL_4030045 obo:PR_000009978) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:CL_4030045 obo:PR_000010543) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:CL_4030045 obo:PR_000010799) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001256) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001257) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001456) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001483) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001879) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001944) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000007597) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0002536) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0002690) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0006909) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0032637)))\n4726:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:068340007X\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D008407\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC1312421\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2855166\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15153310\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16455980\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19671378\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:212366338\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9354811\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000097 \"A cell that is found in almost all tissues containing numerous basophilic granules and capable of releasing large amounts of histamine and heparin upon activation. Progenitors leave bone marrow and mature in connective and mucosal tissue. Mature mast cells are found in all tissues, except the bloodstream. Their phenotype is CD117-high, CD123-negative, CD193-positive, CD200R3-positive, and FceRI-high. Stem-cell factor (KIT-ligand; SCF) is the main controlling signal of their survival and development.\")\n4734:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000097 \"Mast cells are generally integrin beta-7-negative and positive for TLR2, TLR3, TLR4, TLR5, TLR7, TLR9, C3aR, C5aR, CR3, CR4, VEGF, FGF2, and renin. They can express MHC Class I and II on their surface. Activated murine mast cells (IgE+Antigen) were capable of expressing the following co-stimulatory molecules: CD95 (Fas), CD120b, CD137 (4-1BB), CD153 (CD30L), CD154 (CD40L), GITR, ICOSL, OX40L, PD-L1, and PD-L2. Note that there was some mouse strain variation. Mast cells have also been demonstrated to produce bFGF, CCL2, CCL4, CCL5, CCL11, CCL20, CXCL2, CXCL8, CXCL10, GM-CSF, IFN-gamma, IL-1, IL-2, IL-3, IL-8, IL-10, IL-11, IL-12, IL-13, IL-16, IL-25, IL-18, MIP-1, prostaglandin D2, SCF, TGF-beta, TNF-alpha, TSLP, VEGF, and XCL1. They express the transcription factors Transcription factors AP-1, GATA1, MITF, Notch2, PIAS3, PU.1, and STAT5.\")\n4736:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000097 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000766 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:GO_0030141) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:CL_4030046 obo:PR_000001865) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001255) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000006169) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0002349) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0002539) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0002660) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0002690) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0002830) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0030210) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0015015 obo:PR_000002065) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0015015 obo:PR_000007431)))\n4748:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000098 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000066 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0050906)))\n4780:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000101 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000540 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0050906)))\n4839:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000108 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000540 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0014055)))\n4853:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000110 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0002790))\n4874:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000112 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0007601))\n4924:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000118 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000099 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000053 obo:PATO_0070002) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534)))\n4966:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000121 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\n5054:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000129 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000125 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001017) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001012) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0