omeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0046879)))\n17466:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14592528\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002318 \"A mesothelial cell capable of circulating in the blood by first losing its squamous character. This cell can incorporate into the regenerating mesothelium.\")\n17660:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18719589\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002335 \"A preadipocyte that is capable of differentiating into a brown adipocyte. This cell type expresses uncoupling protein-1, PPAR-gamma, PR-domain-containing 16; and PGC-1alpha (peroxisome proliferator-activated receptor-gamma (PPARgamma) coactivator-1alpha).\")\n17683:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0002337 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0036334))\n17774:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19949422\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002347 \"A mature natural killer cell that is CD27-high and CD11b-high. This cell type is capable of interferon-gamma secretion.\")\n17778:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002347 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000824 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_10090) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0032609) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0015015 obo:PR_000001012) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0015015 obo:PR_000001963)))\n17913:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0813817986\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20711979\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002361 \"A progenitor cell that is capable of forming colonies of primitive erythrocytes in the blood island of the yolk sac. First arrive at E7.5 in mouse and expresses CD41.\")\n18072:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35815410\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0002375 \"Schwann cell precursor are capable of differentiating into Schwann cells and other cell types such as melanocytes, neurons, and mesenchymal cells.\")\n18241:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0002394 \"Markers are found in human cells. Normally they represent 3-5% of peripheral blood mDCs (human). These cells express high levels of CD283 (TLR3), are capable of producing IL-12p70 and IFN-beta upon stimulation, and inducing a TH1 response [PMCID:PMC2882828]. They are also Necl2-positive. May be human equivalent of murine CD8-alpha-positive DCs.\")\n18243:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002394 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000782 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000002105) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0002827) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0032606) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0042590)))\n18296:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002399 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000782 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000002027) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0032637)))\n18858:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0002453 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0030154))\n19199:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002488 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000351 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000053 obo:PATO_0000586) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0001974)))\n19228:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002491 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000066 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0050910)))\n19275:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MP:0008894\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002496 \"A T cell that is located in the intestinal epithelium and is capable of a mucosal immune response.\")\n19283:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002496 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0002419 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0001025 obo:UBERON_0001277) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0002385)))\n19566:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0002526 \"They are also CD11c-positive, CD40-positive, CD85j-positive (ILT-2), CD163-positive, CD205-positive (DEC205), CD207-negative (langerin), CD209-positive (DC-SIGN), CD274-positive (PD-L1), CD324-negative (E-cadherin), Factor XIIIa-positive, LOX-I-positive, CLEC6-positive, Dectin-1-positive, and DCIR-positive. Upon stimulation, these cells are capable of producing IL1-beta, IL6, IL8, IL10, IL12p40, IL19, IL20, IL24, TGF-beta, TNF-alpha, GM-CSF, and MCP1. They reside in the dermis.\")\n19568:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002526 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0001006 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:CL_4030046 obo:PR_000002025) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001889) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0045191)))\n19590:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0002529 \"Reside in the dermis. They are also CD11c-positive, CD40-positive, CD207-negative (langerin), CD209-negative (DC-SIGN), and CD324-negative (E-cadherin). When activated, they are capable of producing CXCL8 (IL-8) and IL-15. Possibly a precursor of Langerhans cells or equivalent of langerin-positive dermal DCs in the mouse.\")\n19617:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002532 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000782 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001483) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0032640)))\n20426:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20807818\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9020076\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Endothelial_progenitor_cell&oldid=1069930016\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002619 \"An adult angioblastic cell released from the bone marrow, or from the kidney in some teleost species, capable of blood circulation and participation in angiogenesis by differentiating into blood vessel endothelial cells.\")\n20475:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0002623 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0017156))\n20476:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0002623 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0045087))\n20477:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0002623 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0046541))\n20507:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12898703\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:8734446\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002627 \"A mature astrocyte that is capable of producing cytokines.\")\n20526:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11517395\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14612429\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15246020\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16177057\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18396103\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20021364\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002629 \"A mature microglial cell that has changed shape to an amoeboid morphology and is capable of cytokine production and antigen presentation.\")\n20530:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0002629 \"Mature microglia are reportedly CCR2-positive, CD4-positive, CD9-positive, CD11a-positive, CD11b-positive, CD11c-positive, CD13-positive, CD16-positive, CDw17-positive, CD18-positive, CD21-positive, CD26-negative, CD32-positive, CD35-positive, CD36-positive, CD40-positive, CD44-positive, CD45-positive, CD53-positive, CD54-positive, CD56-negative, CD58-positive, CD63-positive, CD64-positive, CD66-positive, CD80-positive, CD86-positive, CD87-positive, CD92-positive, CD106-positive, CD107a-positive, CD147-positive, CD155-positive, CD162-positive, CD163-positive, CD171-negative, CD200R-positive, CXCR3-positive, CX3CR1-positive, fibronectin-positive, GD3-positive, GLUT1-positive, GLUT3-negative, GLUT5-positive, MHCI-positive, MHCII-positive, P2X4-positive, RFD7-negative, RGS5-negative, alpha-SMA-negative, vimentin-positive, and vwf-negative. Mature microglia are capable of producing BDNF, CCL3, CCL5, CCL7, CCL8, CCL9, CCL19, CCL20,CD40L, CSF, CXCL1, CXCL2, CXCL4, CXCL5, CXCL8, CXCL9, CXCL10, glutamate, IL-1beta, IL-1ra, IL-3, IL-6, IL-10, IL-12, LT, MMP-2, MMP-9, NGF, nitric oxide, ROS, TGF-beta, TNF-alpha.\")\n20532:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002629 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000129 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0001816) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0002536) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0002537) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0006909) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0019882)))\n20785:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002656 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000066 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0002451) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0032940)))\n21008:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20023630\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002679 \"A lymphocyte found in adipose tissue that lacks lineage markers of other lymphocytes but is capable of mediating TH2 cytokine responses. This cell type is found in fat associated lymphoid clusters, proliferates in response to IL2 and produce large amounts of TH2 cytokines such as IL5, IL6 and IL13\")\n21214:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0003014 \"Is capable of brisk transient currents.\")\n22119:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0004232 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0014055))\n22282:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0004245 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0060096))\n22440:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0005011 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0046717))\n22495:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0005018 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000151 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0036321)))\n22503:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0005019 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0008024 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0036321)))\n22550:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0005024 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0014055))\n22717:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ReO:mhb\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0007015 \"OBSOLETE: A cell line cell that is expected to be capable of replicating a limited number of times in culture before undergoing senescence. Mortal cell line cells cannot be propagated indefinitely (as immortal cell line cells can).\")\n22783:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0007021 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0032940))\n22876:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0008011 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000594 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000053 obo:PATO_0001400) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0017145)))\n22894:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008014 \"A motor neuron that is capable of directly inducing muscle contraction.\")\n22901:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008015 \"A motor neuron that is capable of directly inhibiting muscle contraction.\")\n22930:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008019 \"A non-polarised cell precursor cell that is part of some mesenchyme, is associated with the cell matrix but is not connected to other cells and is capable of migration.\")\n22935:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0008019 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0016477))\n22973:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0008025 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000540 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061533)))\n23029:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0008032 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\n23181:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0008048 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061535))\n23220:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0008059 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000540 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061537)))\n23228:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0008060 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000540 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061535)))\n23236:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0008061 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000540 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0014055) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534)))\n24177:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33419165\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Endothelial_colony_forming_cell&oldid=1068242094\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009090 \"An adult endothelial progenitor cell that is resident of adult vasculature and capable of differentiating to regenerate endothelial cell populations. Endothelial colony forming cells are characterised in vivo by clonal proliferative status, de novo vessel formation, homing to ischemic sites and paracrine support of angiogenesis. These cells are phenotypically similar to endothelial cells.\")\n24187:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21181888\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009091 \"A stem cell found in the interstitial compartment of the neonatal testis; it is capable of self-renewal as well as differentiation into steroidogenic cells (adult Leydig cells). Intermediate stages of development include progenitor Leydig cells and immature Leydig cells.\")\n24556:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0010010 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\n24653:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:nv\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MP:0009467\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10711808\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0011003 \"A neurosecretory neuron residing mainly in the hypothalamic supraoptic and paraventricular nuclei and in a number of smaller accessory cell groups between these two nuclei, that is capable of secreting the hormones oxytocin or vasopressin, and sometimes both, into the systemic circulation.\")\n24661:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0011003 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0046879))\n24676:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0011005 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000099 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534)))\n24681:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:nv\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18677503\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:2273099\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0011006 \"A cerebellar interneuron characterized by a spindle-shaped or triangular soma, parasagittally oriented and located at the border between the granular layer and the Purkinje cell layer. The Lugaro cell extends dendrites predominantly in the parasagittal plane, forming synaptic interactions with basket, stellate, and Golgi cells. Its axonal projections extend upward into the molecular layer, where they form a parasagittal plexus and emit long transverse collaterals that run parallel to the long axis of the cerebellar folia. The Lugaro cell is capable of co-releasing GABA and glycine, as evidenced by the expression of glutamate decarboxylase (GAD65/67) and the glycine transporter GlyT2.\")\n24688:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0011006 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\n24689:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0011006 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061537))\n24738:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0011013 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000019 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0097722)))\n24759:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0011016 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0011013 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0030317)))\n24829:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0011024 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0002489 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0050777)))\n24948:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0011105 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0011104 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061527)))\n24957:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0011106 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0011104 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534)))\n24981:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0011109 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000540 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061585)))\n24988:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0011110 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000540 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061538)))\n25030:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0011115 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000000 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0030154)))\n25436:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020003 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\n25467:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020006 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061527))\n25468:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020006 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\n25479:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020007 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0014055))\n25480:SubCl